{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fifth plan-review remediation: narrowed the exemption to routine transient lifecycle checks while preserving all four existing MAJOR safety classes. Expanded the live corpus to five pass and five finding cases so destructive apply, wildcard admin, plaintext secret, and untrusted endpoint behavior are each observed. Added plan-review-T10 to the strict packaged-spec test census, updated file impact, and split compound acceptance items."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786553001197891001,"uuid":"6d7a5efe-cfb8-4935-b85d-d9ec6427b338"}